{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00564",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.01,
      "end_seconds": 10.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "Good morning, Mr Whitcombe. The booking note says you've noticed black stools since starting ibuprofen. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.79,
      "end_seconds": 23.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. Yes, that is right. I have been passing black stools, and it rather alarmed my wife."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.09,
      "end_seconds": 35.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "I'm not surprised. Describe them for me. Is it like tar, or more a dark brown?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.54,
      "end_seconds": 47.23,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "Quite like tar, I would say. Very dark, rather sticky, and unpleasant to flush away, if you will forgive me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.91,
      "end_seconds": 53.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "And when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.14,
      "end_seconds": 66.7,
      "duration_seconds": 10.56,
      "text": "I'm afraid I cannot say with any confidence. Possibly last week, possibly the week before. I did not make a note."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.75,
      "end_seconds": 77.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "That's fine, plenty of people don't. Now, tell me about the ibuprofen. Who started you on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.16,
      "end_seconds": 91.36,
      "duration_seconds": 12.2,
      "text": "My GP prescribed it for my knees. I take the 400 milligrams, I believe. The box is on the kitchen shelf, I'm afraid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.04,
      "end_seconds": 99.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "And how often are you meant to take them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.67,
      "end_seconds": 112.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.27,
      "text": "Three times a day, with food. I take them every day, though I must admit I often forget the lunchtime one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.97,
      "end_seconds": 127.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.37,
      "text": "Right. Think of ibuprofen as a bit of sandpaper on the lining of your stomach. Fine for a while, but it can wear that lining thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.75,
      "end_seconds": 137.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.44,
      "text": "I see. I had rather assumed that taking it with food made it perfectly safe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.22,
      "end_seconds": 147.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "It helps a little, but it doesn't make it safe. Have you been sick at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.78,
      "end_seconds": 155.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "No, not once. I have felt quite well in that respect."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.77,
      "end_seconds": 163.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Good. Any pain in the stomach, even a dull ache after meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.0,
      "end_seconds": 171.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "No pain at all, which is partly why I put off coming."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.17,
      "end_seconds": 179.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Fair enough. What about dizziness, say when you stand up quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.91,
      "end_seconds": 188.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "No, I have been quite steady on my feet, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.64,
      "end_seconds": 195.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Is the ibuprofen your only regular medicine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.54,
      "end_seconds": 205.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Yes, just that one. I try to avoid taking tablets where I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.37,
      "end_seconds": 213.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Any other health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.47,
      "end_seconds": 223.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Osteoarthritis, which is the reason for the knees. And I have high cholesterol, but I manage that with diet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.3,
      "end_seconds": 231.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Sensible. And how are the knees managing generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.39,
      "end_seconds": 240.9,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Stiff in the mornings, but they loosen up. Ibuprofen takes the edge off, I will say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.22,
      "end_seconds": 246.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Understood. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.44,
      "end_seconds": 257.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "One. I had a hernia repair, about twelve years ago. It went very smoothly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.46,
      "end_seconds": 271.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.65,
      "text": "You said you take it with food. Do you take it with a drink of any sort, milk or tea perhaps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.01,
      "end_seconds": 282.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.87,
      "text": "Just a cup of tea with my breakfast. Nothing more elaborate than that, I'm afraid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.89,
      "end_seconds": 293.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Good. Let me check you over. I'll take your pulse and blood pressure first, then feel your tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.53,
      "end_seconds": 298.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Of course. Shall I roll up my sleeve?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.41,
      "end_seconds": 331.18,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "Yes please. Pulse is 92, blood pressure 118 over 74, oxygen level 98 percent, and your temperature is 36.8 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.48,
      "end_seconds": 335.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Are those numbers all right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.88,
      "end_seconds": 347.07,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "They're acceptable, nothing that worries me today. Now, lie back for me, and tell me if anything is sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.01,
      "end_seconds": 352.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Certainly. It's perfectly comfortable so far."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.67,
      "end_seconds": 376.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Your tummy feels soft all the way round, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.02,
      "end_seconds": 385.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "That is a relief. May I ask what happens now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.84,
      "end_seconds": 396.11,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "I'd rather not put a name on this just yet. But the first step is simple. Stop the ibuprofen from today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.33,
      "end_seconds": 403.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Understood. Should I simply stop it altogether, or cut down?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 405.96,
      "end_seconds": 415.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Stop it altogether, and don't swap it for any similar painkiller from the chemist either. Those cause the same trouble."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.17,
      "end_seconds": 423.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "I shall be careful about that. My knees may complain, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.26,
      "end_seconds": 432.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "They might, and we can talk about gentler options for them another time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.91,
      "end_seconds": 441.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Thank you. Is there anything I should watch for in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.54,
      "end_seconds": 455.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.66,
      "text": "Yes. If the stools stay black, or you feel faint, or you bring up blood, go to A and E straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 457.78,
      "end_seconds": 463.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "I will, doctor. I'll let my wife know as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 464.2,
      "end_seconds": 470.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Good idea. She sounds sensible. Mind how you go, Mr Whitcombe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.32,
      "end_seconds": 475.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Thank you very much. Good morning."
    }
  ]
}
